Moved PulpBot from the decommissioned Splunk to Sumo Logic: the entrypoint no longer exports `SPLUNK_TOKEN`, a new credential-holding `sumo-search` helper reads `SUMO_API_URL`, `SUMO_ACCESS_ID` and `SUMO_ACCESS_KEY` straight from the `agent-pulpbot` Secret and runs bounded Search Job API queries (7-day window, 1000 rows, 28000-byte output), `secret-guard` now treats `*ACCESS_KEY*`/`*ACCESS_ID*` variables as secrets and blocks `declare`/`typeset`/`export -p NAME`, and the charter points PulpBot at Sumo Logic for logs.
